    <div class="page">
        <h2 class="section-title">P.A.W.S Orientation</h2>
        <p>P.A.W.S., which stands for <span data-field="paws_full_name">{{ paws_full_name }}</span>, is Fisk University's new student onboarding program that requires the participation of all new students enrolling Fall {{ enrollment_year }}. P.A.W.S. supports new students in making a successful transition to college and becoming acclimated to the campus community by providing them with opportunities to participate in various programs and events.</p>
        <p>P.A.W.S consists of programs and activities that:</p>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc;">
            <li class="bullet-point">provide first-year and transfer students opportunities to network with their future classmates, prepare for life inside and outside the classroom, and learn to navigate campus life.</li>
            <li class="bullet-point">support and answer questions about academics, health, safety, college transitions, engagement, and support services through workshops, programs, and speaker series.</li>
            <li class="bullet-point">provide an opportunity to meet with academic departments, an overview of university resources and technology, and a chance to interact with multiple university offices supporting the Fisk University journey.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

